  "notes": "Bemba (Chibemba, Guthrie M.42), Bantu language of the Northern, Luapula and Copperbelt provinces of Zambia. Five vowel qualities a/e/i/o/u with a phonemic length distinction, not marked in the standard orthography. Prenasalized voiceless and voiced series (mp/mb, nt/nd, ntʃ/ndʒ, nk/ng, plus prenasalized fricatives mf, ns, nsh) are single phonemes. ⟨ng'⟩ /ŋ/ is the bare velar nasal, contrasting with prenasalized ⟨ng⟩ /ᵑɡ/, the same convention as Nyanja and Yao. /b/ has the intervocalic fricative allophone [β]. Bemba is tonal (two register tones, H/L) but tone is not marked in the standard orthography and carries a comparatively low functional load.",
